From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] build/config: unwindlib must match rtlib on riscv64

3.50.0 added --unwindlib=libunwind to the custom libcxx link flags for
linux. riscv64 builds the engine with the native clang rather than the
bundled one, because the bundled one cannot link there, and the native
clang defaults to --rtlib=libgcc. clang refuses the pair:

  clang++: error: --rtlib=libgcc requires --unwindlib=libgcc

Point the flag at the unwinder that matches the rtlib actually in use.
The recipe's ABI interop gate already expects libgcc_s on this
configuration and says so in its rule 4 note, so this is the deviation
the recipe chose, spelled out on the link line.

Scoped to riscv64 through SRC_URI, since every other target links with
the bundled clang, where upstream's libunwind is correct.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific toolchain combination]

Signed-off-by: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
---
 engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn b/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
--- a/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -648,8 +648,10 @@
 
     if (is_linux) {
       # Our custom libcxx doesn't include the unwinder, which is included in
-      # libc++.a. Link the libunwind directly.
-      ldflags += [ "--unwindlib=libunwind" ]
+      # libc++.a. Link the unwinder that matches the rtlib in use: this
+      # target builds with the native clang, which defaults to
+      # --rtlib=libgcc, and clang rejects that paired with libunwind.
+      ldflags += [ "--unwindlib=libgcc" ]
     }
   }
 
-- 
2.52.0
